Patch: 0002-defined-config-and-strict-parsing.patch
Applies to: native/vendor/dungeonmaker-2.05/DungeonMaker.cpp (after 0001)
What: Config's constructors give every scalar field a defined value (0/false), and
  Config::AcceptDesign returns false as soon as a read fails: at the top of the main loop,
  after every read inside a list loop, and for unknown SquareData/Direction tokens (which
  now set failbit instead of leaving the target uninitialized).
Why: A design missing a record (T, M, N, PR, PT, PU, U, ...) left Config fields
  uninitialized, so the same text and seed produced different dungeons per compiler and
  even per call (spec section 5.3). A non-numeric token or a list without terminator made
  the parser loop forever or grow memory without bound (spec section 5.4). Valid designs
  parse exactly as before.
Date: 2026-10-31
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

